  "id": "COMPOUND:17321 - PROTEIN:472",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which cis-4-Methoxycinnamic acid may interact with Phosphatidylserine synthase 1, through a series of molecular targets. The compound is linked to Fatty-acid amide hydrolase 1, which is a target of (2S)-2-(4-chlorophenoxy)-3-phenylpropanoic acid and also of 3a-Methyl-7-methylidene-1-(propan-2-yl)decahydro-4,8-epithioazulene. Both of these compounds are known to interact with Phosphatidylserine synthase 1, indicating a possible pathway where cis-4-Methoxycinnamic acid may modulate the activity of this enzyme. Additionally, cis-4-Methoxycinnamic acid is linked to BT-549, which is a target of Skim milk, and Skim milk is also a target of Phosphatidylserine synthase 1. This suggests that the compound may influence the enzyme through a chain of molecular interactions, potentially affecting phospholipid synthesis. The evidence is consistent with a mechanistic link, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
